# DURABLE REPRO — B7: `&` applied to a NON-PLACE.
#
# `&make().fd` takes a mutable borrow of a field of a temporary that dies at the
# end of the statement. There is nothing for the callee to write through TO.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C and LLVM): `gg check` is clean, the
# program builds and runs, and the write goes into the doomed temporary — a dead
# write the user asked to be visible. `ggdef` REJECTS: "expression is not a
# place".
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check`. D31 full-strict defines `&` as "the callee
# writes through", which presupposes a place to write through to; `make()` is a
# value. This is the same predicate as the `E_LocalBorrowBind` control
# (`sound_amp_named_bind_control.gg`) applied one step earlier — the operand,
# not the destination.
#
# The `fd` seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, so the dead write is a real store
# rather than something const-folding can erase.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the `&`-of-a-non-place row of the
# `&`-in-an-owning-position filing.
struct Cell:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 7

Cell make():
    return Cell(seed())

void bumpint(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    bumpint(&make().fd)
    print("survived")
